>The disk accessing seems to be a common complaint.  The cure - use whatever
>extra memory you have as a disk cache, not a ramdisk.  Give it a try!

Actually, you should get the best performance by not using the memory at
all.  The C7 Move overlay manager will cache overlays itself based on
the following algorithm:

	1) If the desired overlay is in conventional memory use it.

	Else, we assume we must discard an overlay to make room

	2) If the overlay is already cached, discard it.
	3) If there is sufficient XMS memory, cache to XMS.
	4) If there is sufficient EMS memory, cache to EMS.
	5) Discard and reload from disk next time needed.

Thus, if you have XMS (i.e. Himem.sys or 386Max or others) or EMS
memory available, the overlay manager will use it to cache overlays.
This should be faster than trying to cache the disk hits involved.

